      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Heights%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the Pittsburgh and Lake Erie Railroad opened a station there, the town was renamed Shannopin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Heights%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "South Heights sits on the Ohio River in southeastern Beaver County, Pennsylvania.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Heights%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The borough borders Hopewell Township to the north, south and west, and Crescent Township in Allegheny County to the southwest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Heights%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Across the Ohio River to the east, South Heights shares a border with the borough of Ambridge.",
